 "conventions": "CR1b shared world (QuantMind 10-14 approval of CR1b; order V4_COMBO_V1_CR1 s3; contract V4). New file;\ncr1_common (CR1's run record), v4_world, m1_ruler, m2h_* are imported, never modified.\n\nSame as CR1 (cr1_common docstring): the 8-cell combo fit on the A half with real labels, the A/B halves,\nthe worlds (real / null / p8 / p32), the ruler (rank_weights -> held_path H168 -> delisting layer ->\nsettle_multi, flat6 / cost0, lag 1), the marginal = log NAV(combo + f) - log NAV(combo) per tile.\nChanged:\n  residual  the formula's TOP100 rank z per tile row is regressed per hour on the 8 cells' z (OLS with\n            intercept over the coins where z_f is finite and the combo is defined; a missing cell z\n            enters as 0, its cross-sectional mean); the residual, re-standardised (>= 20 coins), is the\n            ninth equal-weight cell: (N + r_f) / (K + 1). Only what the 8 cells do not hold is rewarded.\n  plant     s_perp8 = the plant formula's rank z residualised the same way on every tile row, so the\n            plant formula's own residual is s_perp8; fwd[t] += alpha s_perp8[t-1]; alpha from s_perp8\n            alone (full book, cost0, A tiles) = +8 / +32 bp/day.\n  corr_s    Spearman of the residual r_f with s_perp8 (corr_raw: the raw signal with s_perp8, reported).\n  books     every decision (pre-run checks, frozen set, NULL bar, found) on the K10 book net only\n            (QuantMind E3: K10/K20 are the books we trade; ADR-0009 conc_k10_net). K20 and full are\n            reported, never gated. Training reward = A-half marginal full-book net (CR1's; a training\n            signal, not a gate).\n",
 "checks": "CR1b step 0 and pre-run checks (QuantMind 10-14 CR1b approval, points 1-2; AGENTS.md veto rule). V4 TRAIN\nonly; no DEV, no OOS. Refuses if CR1B_ALPHA.json exists. Written before any CR1b number.\n\n  orth     per hour corr of s_perp8 with C and with each active cell's z over the regression sample:\n           max mean |corr| < 0.05 (the residual is orthogonal by construction; this checks the code).\n  alpha    s_perp8 alone, full book, cost0, mean over the 30 A tiles: lift over the real world = +8 / +32\n           bp/day (within 2 %), secant from CR1's p8 alpha.\n  visible  p8 world, the plant formula as the residualised ninth cell, B half: marginal net mean > 0,\n           t >= 2, corr_s(B) > 0.7.\n  rank     p8 world, B half: the plant formula's rank among the 50 CR1 PC candidates\n           (CR1_PC_P8\\ROUND_PC.json, a pool a marginal-reward trainer actually reached in a p8 world)\n           re-scored under the CR1b marginal, same book: rank <= 10 (rank = 1 + candidates strictly above).\n  book     decisions on concentrated books only (QuantMind E3). Declared now: rank_book = conc_k10 if K10\n           passes visible and rank; else conc_k20 if K20 passes both; else no launch, hand to the user\n           (no other fallback, no alpha / pool / threshold change).\n  reported the plant row in real / null / p8 / p32 x K10 / K20 / full x A / B; the candidates' max in the\n           NULL world (a proxy of the NULL bar, not a gate).\n\n    python -I cr1b_calib.py     rc 0 launch, 6 alpha, 7 not visible, 8 orthogonality, 9 rank > 10\n",
